 ],
 "literal": "At the mountain cleft cave range, to the might-possessing goddess with a trident, / vows we will not undertake, hand-thread we will not tie; / bird omens we will not examine, voice-omens we will not wait for; / even thinking of us he does not think, indeed, O friend! / Since he was like life to life, than themselves / even for the duration of a blink not abiding, towards us / having forgotten, there staying is possible only for those capable ones.",
 "translation": "We will not make vows to the mighty goddess of the trident who resides in the mountain clefts, nor will we tie the protective thread on our wrists. We will not look for bird omens, nor wait for favorable voices. He does not even think of us, my friend! He who was like life to our life, who could not bear to be parted from us even for the blink of an eye, has now forgotten us and stays there. Only those with strong hearts are capable of doing that.",
 "modern": "தோழியே! மலைப்பிளவுகளின் குகைகளில் வாழும் வலிமை மிக்க சூலமேந்திய கொற்றவைக்கு நாம் நேர்த்திக்கடன் செலுத்த மாட்டோம்; கையில் காப்பு நாணும் கட்ட மாட்டோம். பறவைகளின் சகுனங்களை ஆராய மாட்டோம்; விரிச்சி கேட்டு நிற்கவும் மாட்டோம். நம் காதலர் நம்மைப் பற்றிச் சிறிதும் நினைக்கவே இல்லை. நம் உயிருக்கு உயிராக இருந்தவர், கண் இமைக்கும் நேரம் கூட நம்மைப் பிரிய ஆற்றாதவர், இப்போது நம்மை மறந்து அங்கேயே தங்கியிருப்பது நெஞ்சுறுதி படைத்தவர்களால்தான் இயலும்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine speaks to her confidante (தோழி) in this pālai (wasteland) poem, expressing her deep grief over her husband's prolonged absence. Her family or friends might suggest performing rituals to the goddess Sūli (Kotravai), tying protective threads, or looking for omens to ease her worry. She rejects all these rituals as futile because the hero has completely forgotten her. She contrasts his past behavior—when he was so loving that he could not bear to part from her even for the blink of an eye—with his current ability to stay away so long. She bitterly concludes that only those with exceptionally hard hearts (valliyōr) can forget their beloved and live apart like this.",
